  "term": "quantum",
  "definition": "In cognition, quantum refers to a way of modelling mental and brain processes with quantum-style probability and state-space concepts rather than classical ones. In this usage, it points to context-sensitive, non-commutative changes in cognitive states, where observation or judgment can alter the state being described.",
